  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "All seven choices rose over five years, with Amazon leading this set. Moody’s and AIG also gained strongly from this starting date. AIG’s chart includes an extraordinary jump of about 245% in August 2009, plus sharp falls at other times. Starting after a collapse can produce striking gains, but recovery was not guaranteed.\n\nThe next years included the Deepwater Horizon disaster, Japan’s earthquake and tsunami, and the landing of Curiosity on Mars. Life did not stop while markets recovered. Scientific achievements and terrible disasters appeared alongside business news during the holding period.\n\nA percentage gain needs a starting amount. Doubling a share after a huge earlier fall may still leave a long-time owner far below what they originally paid. Your game investment begins in March 2009, so it does not include those earlier losses. That makes the starting date essential to the story. The large gains here are real within this example, but they should not be confused with a promise that every damaged company will recover.",
    "source_ids": [
      "french-us",
      "french-international",
      "fred-gs5",
      "yahoo-aig",
      "yahoo-mco",
      "yahoo-amzn",
